I thought that melee with Mjolnir destroyed potions as well as wands in
monsterinventories?  It's part of why I have liked to evolve away from
using it in the late game.

> Before you get strength bonuses and scrolls of enchant weapon,
> Mjollnir is probably the most damaging weapon out there.  I really
> like Grayswandir, but at +0 and strength 14, can anything beat Mojo?

Its shock damage makes it the biggest hitter at +0.  As the game
progresses more and more of the monsters are shock resistant and it's
only a war hammer to them.  Regular war hammer is a very poor weapon. 
So as the game progresses and the enchantment expectations increase,
several other artifacts are better when highly enchanted.

> I almost never throw Mjollnir.  As a valk I might if there's a mind
> flayer a few squares away and I don't care much about my rings, but
> you have to come up with a narrow set of parameters where throwing
> Mojo is better than all of your other options (like burning Elbereth
> with a wand of fire and then using wands/missiles/daggers).

With a valkyrie I'll want a good artifact long sword and spend much of
the game throwing daggers and hitting with Excalibur, Vorpal Blade or
one of the Brands.  I've tried throwing Mjolnir across the Castle
drawbridge and it works great until that time when it hits you on the
way back and explodes a ring.  Then it's on the ground in front of you
and there's still an advancing horde of monsters.  Time to switch to
that big stack of highly enchanted daggers.  When facing the drawbridge
with any class that can multifire daggers I carry a *lot* of them to
face the drawbridge.

> Anyway, I am utterly convinced that Mjollnir is one of the better
